  "userGuide": "Using the app",
  "guideAddTitle": "Add an account",
  "guideAddBody": "Choose Add to scan a setup QR code, select a supported image, or enter the setup key. Verify a code with the service before removing your previous method.",
  "guideCodesTitle": "Use your codes",
  "guideCodesBody": "Enter the current code at the service. Time-based codes change automatically; counter-based codes can be advanced manually. Search, categories, and sorting help organize accounts.",
  "guideBackupTitle": "Keep a backup",
  "guideBackupBody": "Export a password-protected backup and store it safely. Test recovery before replacing your device. Unencrypted exports and QR codes reveal account secrets.",
  "guideMigrationTitle": "Move existing accounts",
  "guideMigrationBody": "Choose Add to import a supported file or follow the migration guides. Imports show a confirmation and conflict policy before saving.",
  "welcomeTitle": "Welcome",
  "welcomeIntro": "Set up verification codes, keep a protected backup, and retain recovery options for your accounts.",
  "getStarted": "Get started",
  "aboutApp": "About",
  "aboutDescription": "An offline app for managing verification codes.",
  "sourceCode": "Source code",
  "openSourceLicenses": "Open-source licenses",
  "aboutPrivacy": "Account secrets are encrypted on this device. Exported files and QR codes may reveal them.",
  "googleGuide": "On the old device, open Google Authenticator, choose the menu, then Transfer codes (or Transfer accounts) and Export. Unlock the device, select the accounts, and continue to display the QR code.\n\nIn this app, return to Add and choose Scan QR code. Scan every code from the same export; this app asks for confirmation after the complete batch is received. Check the import summary and verify codes with the services before removing the old setup.\n\nThe QR codes contain account secrets. Keep them private. Camera support varies by platform; unsupported or incomplete batches are not imported. If the old device is unavailable, use each service’s recovery options.\n\nOfficial help: https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/1066447"
}
